### ============================================
### Auth0 Flask App - Test Suite
### For Lab: Securing and Monitoring Flask App
### ============================================

### 1. TEST PUBLIC ACCESS (Should work without login)
### ============================================

# Test Home Page (Public)
GET http://localhost:5000/
Accept: text/html

# Test Health Endpoint
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. TEST UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS (Should redirect to login)
### ============================================

# Test Protected Route Without Login - Should redirect to /login
GET http://localhost:5000/protected
Accept: text/html

# Test Profile Without Login - Should redirect to /login
GET http://localhost:5000/profile
Accept: text/html

### 3. TEST AUTH0 LOGIN FLOW (Valid Authentication)
### ============================================

# Step 1: Initiate Login - Redirects to Auth0
GET http://localhost:5000/login
Accept: text/html

# Step 2: Auth0 Callback (After successful login)
# Note: This will be handled automatically by Auth0 redirect
# After login, you'll be redirected back to: http://localhost:5000/callback?code=xxx&state=yyy
GET http://localhost:5000/callback?code=test_code&state=test_state
Accept: text/html

### 4. TEST PROTECTED ACCESS (Valid - After Login)
### ============================================

# Test Protected Route with Authentication
# You need to be logged in first (get session cookie)
# The session cookie is automatically handled by your browser
GET http://localhost:5000/protected
Accept: text/html
# Expected: 200 OK - Access granted

# Test Profile with Authentication
GET http://localhost:5000/profile
Accept: text/html
# Expected: 200 OK - Access granted

### 5. TEST EXCESSIVE ACCESS (Simulate Traffic)
### ============================================

# Access Protected Route 15+ times to trigger alert
# Run this 15+ times in a row with valid authentication
# Each should return 200 OK
GET http://localhost:5000/protected
Accept: text/html
# Expected: 200 OK for each request

# Alternative: Access Protected Route with delay (simulates real user)
# Wait 1-2 seconds between requests to simulate human behavior
# After 10+ accesses in 15 minutes, KQL query should detect it

### 6. TEST LOGOUT
### ============================================

# Logout - Clear session and redirect to Auth0 logout
GET http://localhost:5000/logout
Accept: text/html
# Expected: 302 Redirect to Auth0 logout page

### 7. SIMULATE BRUTE FORCE / SUSPICIOUS ACTIVITY
### ============================================

# Rapid successive accesses (simulates automated attack)
# Uncomment and run these in quick succession
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected
# GET http://localhost:5000/protected

### 8. TEST AZURE DEPLOYMENT (After Deployment)
### ============================================

# For testing on Azure, replace localhost with your Azure URL:
# GET https://auth0-flask-monitor.azurewebsites.net/
# GET https://auth0-flask-monitor.azurewebsites.net/health
# GET https://auth0-flask-monitor.azurewebsites.net/protected

### 9. TEST API ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

# Check if the app is healthy
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json
# Expected: {"status":"healthy"}

### 10. VERIFY LOGGING
### ============================================

# After running these tests, check your terminal for log entries like:
# SECURITY_EVENT: {"event_type": "login_success", ...}
# SECURITY_EVENT: {"event_type": "protected_access", ...}
# SECURITY_EVENT: {"event_type": "unauthorized_access", ...}

### ============================================
### End of Test Suite
### ============================================
